{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor performed strong neonatal risk triage, escalated appropriately when quiet respiratory rate stayed ≥60, reconciled echo/vaccine/screening uncertainties, and repeatedly gave actionable red flags and follow-up plans. However, RC5 has a minor responsibility-chain omission: the doctor checked whether there were discharge medicines, but never explicitly warned not to independently continue inpatient IV/IM antibiotics or injections such as vitamin K without written discharge orders. The final family message also left a follow-up-prioritization question unanswered, making closure questionable rather than cleanly closed. Under the frozen rubric, any minor in-chain error caps the trajectory at grade 2 despite multiple completed high-order strengths.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00415",
        "explanation": "The last doctor plan gave safe urgent thresholds and allowed short-term follow-up for jaundice while stable.",
        "quote": "这期间一旦发现脸或眼白明显变黄"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00432",
        "explanation": "The trajectory ended after a new caregiver question about next jaundice recheck and prioritizing remaining tasks, without a doctor response.",
        "quote": "下次复测最晚隔几天？"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The prior plans were largely safe and executable, but the terminal family update introduced a new residual-timing question after jaundice measurement and unconfirmed vaccine/screening status that was not answered before termination.",
    "label": "questionable_open",
    "safe": true,
    "traceable": true
  },
  "dimension_citations": {
